      "description": "Watch Fenerbahce vs Sturm Graz highlights and goals from UEFA Champions League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 5, 2026. The high-stakes atmosphere of the UEFA Champions League set the stage for a compelling encounter on August 5, 2026 . Both Fenerbahce and Sturm Graz took to the pitch with clear ambitions, knowing that every tactical decision could define their European journey. Early Breakthrough in Istanbul Fenerbahce wasted no time in establishing their presence on the field. In the 10th minute, a moment of individual brilliance combined with teamwork saw Kerem Akturkoglu provide a clinical assist for Anderson Talisca , who buried his chance to score the opening goal . The home crowd erupted as their side took control of the match . Sturm Graz struggled to contain the pressure, and Jon Gorenc-Stankovic saw a yellow card in the 21st minute as the visitors tried to halt the momentum. Doubling the Lead Before the Break Despite an early injury setback that forced Jayden Oosterwolde off for Archie Brown , the hosts remained relentless. As the first half reached its conclusion, a second blow was dealt to the Austrian side. In the 45th minute, Marco Asensio turned provider, finding Mason Greenwood , who calmly converted to make it 2-0. This late strike just before half-time gave Fenerbahce a commanding cushion heading into the tunnel. Solid Management and Final Whistle The second half saw a flurry of tactical changes as Sturm Graz attempted to fight back, introducing several substitutes like Axel Kayombo and Ryan Fosso . However, the rhythm of the game favored the hosts, who managed the tempo effectively. Yellow cards for Juergen Heil and Kayombo further hindered the visitors' progress. Fenerbahce utilized their bench depth, bringing on Fred and Irfan Kahveci to maintain stability. The referee blew the final whistle at 90+4', confirming a professional and well-earned victory for the home side."
